[38;2;124;124;124m{φ_n} is a definable sequence of formulas), then f is definable by recursion, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mand ZFC proves the existence of f as a set (by the recursion theorem, since ω is[0m[38;2;124;124;124ma set).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWait, but the reflection theorem gives us that the class of reflecting ordinals [0m[38;2;124;124;124mis closed unbounded. "The least reflecting ordinal greater than β" is definable [0m[38;2;124;124;124mif "reflecting ordinal for φ_n" is definable. And it is, for each fixed n, since[0m[38;2;124;124;124mφ_n is a specific formula.[0m

