[38;2;124;124;124mstrictly increasing sequence {β_n} where each φ_n reflects at V_{β_n}.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mBut the question says "each subformula of φ_n is absolute for V_{β_n}". The [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mreflection theorem already handles this: when we say φ reflects at V_β, the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mstandard proof ensures all subformulas reflect. Actually, the standard statement[0m[38;2;124;124;124mis that φ and all its subformulas are absolute for V_β. Or more precisely, the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtheorem produces β such that φ is absolute for V_β, and the proof ensures this [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mby making all subformulas absolute.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me be more careful. The Lévy reflection theorem says: for any [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mformula φ, there is a closed unbounded class C of ordinals such that for all β [0m
[38;2;124;124;124min C, φ is absolute for V_β. The proof works by showing each subformula has a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mclosed unbounded class of reflecting ordinals, and taking the finite [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mintersection.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo "all subformulas of φ_n are absolute for V_{β_n}" is exactly what the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mreflection theorem gives us.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the answer is: Yes, it is possible, and this is provable in ZFC.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe construction: Given a sequence of formulas {φ_n}, define β_n recursively:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- β_0 = the least ordinal β such that all subformulas of φ_0 are absolute for [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mV_β[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- β_{n+1} = the least ordinal β > β_n such that all subformulas of φ_{n+1} are [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mabsolute for V_β[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mBy the Lévy reflection theorem (provable in ZFC), the class of ordinals where [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mall subformulas of φ_n are absolute is closed unbounded, so such β always exists[0m[38;2;124;124;124mand can be chosen > β_n. The recursion theorem in ZFC (applied to the set ω) [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mgives us the function n ↦ β_n as a set.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me write this up as a clean proof.[0m

